# Line-ending normalisation — critical for cross-platform work (finding P0-003).
# Bash scripts and Node.js MUST be stored with LF: otherwise a checkout on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true gives them CRLF, and on Linux/macOS the shebang breaks
# (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` -> `bash: bad interpreter: No such file or directory`).
#
# This file is published verbatim, so it is written in English like everything else in the public
# tree. Until v1.19.0 it was in Russian and the export language gate never looked at it: the gate
# selected files by extension, and a name with no extension matched nothing. The gate now decides
# by content.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts and data — always LF
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.mjs       text eol=lf
*.js        text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
# The Stop hook has no extension — an explicit rule
ralph-loop-stop text eol=lf

# Windows-specific wrappers — CRLF
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf

# Binary files — no normalisation
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary

# Raw archived tool output is evidence; preserve its original whitespace.
docs/reports/1.28.0_audit_round*_archive/**/*.log -whitespace
